rr_bridge.dll: the NGX bridge of REFramework-RayReconstruction
==============================================================

REFramework, and the source code of this bridge, are under the MIT license (LICENSE at the root of the
repository). This notice covers what the bridge takes from NVIDIA when it is built with the NVIDIA DLSS
SDK, that is, with the CMake variable RR_DLSS_SDK_DIR pointing to a clone of
https://github.com/NVIDIA/DLSS at v310.9.16.

Parts of NVIDIA
---------------

Built that way, rr_bridge.dll incorporates, in object code form, portions of the NVIDIA NGX SDK of the
DLSS SDK: the static library nvsdk_ngx_s.lib (nvsdk_ngx_s_dbg.lib in a Debug build) and the inline
helpers of its headers. Those portions are not under the MIT license. They are licensed under the
NVIDIA RTX SDKs License, which the build copies next to this file as NVIDIA_RTX_SDKs_LICENSE.txt, from
LICENSE.txt in the clone. None of NVIDIA's files is part of the REFramework-RayReconstruction
repository.

This software contains source code provided by NVIDIA Corporation.

The snippet of DLSS Ray Reconstruction
--------------------------------------

nvngx_dlssd.dll belongs to NVIDIA Corporation and is governed by the same license. Neither the
repository nor its releases include or distribute it. Whoever installs RR takes it from
lib/Windows_x86_64/rel/ of NVIDIA/DLSS at v310.9.16 and places it in reframework/rr/ next to the
bridge: by hand, with install_rr_snippet.bat, which downloads it from there and checks it, or by
letting the build copy it from the clone (the CMake option RR_COPY_DLSSD_SNIPPET).

